 Then there exist positive constants $\bar\gg$, $\bar\tau$, and $\bar\varrho$ such that for any starting point $(x^0,\lm^0)\in \B_{\bar\gg}(\ox,\olm)\cap\big(\Th\times \R^m\big)$
 there is a primal-dual sequence   $\{(\xk,\lk)\c$,  generated by Algorithm~{\rm\ref{Alg1}} with $\rok \ge \bar\varrho$ and   $\ek=\sigma(\xk,\lk)$ for all $k$, where $\sigma$ is defined by \eqref{error}, satisfying the  estimate
